.TH "FWD DOCTOR" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd doctor Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-doctor \- Check local prerequisites (ssh, rsync, backend CLIs) and
the reachability of each configured target.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd doctor
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check local prerequisites (ssh, rsync, backend CLIs) and the
reachability of each configured target.
.PP
Exits non-zero when a check fails, so it doubles as a preflight in scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t,\fP \-\-target <str>
Check only this target instead of every configured one.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP <auto|rich|markdown|json>
Output format: auto uses Rich in a terminal and Markdown otherwise.
[default: auto]
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fP
Render structured output as JSON; shorthand for --format json.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP means every requested check passed. A nonzero status means at
least one prerequisite or target check failed.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
